  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 AM EDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nA front near the OH River tonight will push southward and cross our \narea during the day. It will have little impact on our sensible \nweather, as warm temperatures will persist behind it for the next \nfew days due to a large mid/upper ridge across the region. Dewpoints \nmay be a little lower behind the front, in the mid 60s to lower 70s, \nwhich may help keep the Heat Index below Advisory values. Southern \nand central Valley locations are expected to see Heat Index values \nof 100 to 105 today and Tuesday. \n\nRain chances will be low through the week, and mainly focused along \nthe higher terrain of the mountains and SW VA. The upper ridge may \nshow signs of weakening around the weekend, which could allow for \nsome better rain chances early next week.",
